A phrase narrating the change rather than the code.
-- hit/doc-comment --
Load reads the manifest. It used to read the lock file too.
Parse returns an error for an empty input; previously it returned nil.
This now correctly rejects a nil key.
Keeps the old behavior for callers that pass a path.
-- pass/doc-comment --
Sign takes the key that is used to sign every envelope, which is what a verifier checks.
Walk reads the directory now, before the caller can change it, instead of deferring the read.
-- pass/doc-comment whole --
Example keeps its command table verbatim:

	tool --previously-set  rerun with the old flag
-- fp/doc-comment --
SignBare pins the case where a purpose after a bare noun reads as a habit, so the key used to sign is reported.
